{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Pin `config.local_to_jira_status` against the canonical Jira-family map\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n**This ticket's original scope is already delivered; what remains is one specific residue, and this\nplan has been rewritten to that residue.** Filed during J1 as \"the local->Jira maps exist in two\ndrifted copies inside `adapters/jira/`\". Story J2 [rebar:62d9-9f6d-ecf4-4743] consolidated those two\ninto a single definition and resolved the drift. Verified against the tree, not assumed:\n\n* `adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py` now holds the SOLE adapter-side definition\n  (`LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA`, `LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA`).\n* The ACLI transport reads it (`acli.py:73,75`; `acli_cli_ops.py:35`) and so does the Backend port\n  (`outbound_fields.py:35-36`), both via an alias to the old private names.\n* The `deleted` drift is decided: the unified map adopts `\"deleted\": \"Done\"`, and\n  `test_acli_status_resolution_heldout.py` pins it\n  (`test_deleted_now_resolves_to_done_instead_of_the_invalid_deleted`).\n\nSo original ACs 1-3 are met. The residue is the **THIRD copy**, which J2 deliberately left out of its\nscope and named this ticket for, in `value_maps.py`'s own module docstring: \"``rebar_reconciler/\nconfig.py``'s separate third copy is deliberately out of this story's scope — see bug\nfe15-3bc4-ed70-4b61.\"\n\n## Evidence — the residue is a REAL unpinned gap, measured\n\n`config.local_to_jira_status` (`config.py:24-38`) is a key-for-key **independent literal**.\nToday it is content-identical to `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` (compared programmatically: `==` is True), so\nthere is no drift *yet* — but nothing prevents one.\n\nMUTATION EXPERIMENT (the same method that originally exposed this bug class): setting\n`config.local_to_jira_status[\"deleted\"] = \"Archived-MUTANT\"` — a value that is NOT a state in the live\nDIG workflow ({To Do, In Progress, In Review, Done}) — left **59 passed, 0 failed** across\n`state/test_config.py`, `test_acli_status_resolution_heldout.py`, `test_jira_family_seam.py`, and\n`test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py`. Nothing catches divergence. That is precisely the failure mode\nthis ticket reported, surviving in the one copy J2 did not touch.\n\nNote the partial existing cover, so this plan does not re-add it: `test_config.py`'s\n`test_idea_maps_to_jira_idea_across_all_status_maps` already pins the `idea -> IDEA` entry across all\nthree maps. It is ONE key. The other six are unpinned, which is why the mutation above went unseen.\n\n## Approach — a parity test, NOT a shared import\n\n**Do not make `config.py` import the canonical map.** `config.py` currently imports nothing but\n`__future__` — it is a deliberately zero-dependency core module — and `adapters/jira_family/` is a\nVENDOR package whose `__init__` states its dependency direction is one-way (\"Concrete backends import\nthis package; it never imports them back\"). Having core `config` import a Jira adapter would invert\nthat layering. It would also put the operator-override surface and the documented empty-dict\nkill-switch (`test_config.py:91-98`) behind an adapter import.\n\n**Use the idiom this file already established for exactly this problem.** `config.jira_to_local_status`\nis a second literal of `inbound_differ._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS`, and the codebase keeps the two honest\nwith a PARITY TEST plus a lock-step comment — see the comment at `config.py:50-51` (\"Must stay in\nlock-step with inbound_differ._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS (parity is enforced by tests/.../test_config.py)\")\nand `test_jira_to_local_status_parity_with_inbound_differ`. Mirror that, one layer over.\n\n`test_config.py` already has the mechanism: `_load_attr(module_file, attr)` loads a constant **from a\nfile path** via `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location`, so the test reads the adapter's map WITHOUT\nimporting the adapter package into core's test context — and it is already called with\n`\"adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py\"` today. No new machinery is needed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_config.py` — ONE new parity test.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py` — a lock-step COMMENT above\n  `local_to_jira_status`, mirroring the one already above `jira_to_local_status`. No code change.\n\n**NOT in scope:** any change to a map's VALUES (they already agree; changing one would be a behaviour\nchange this ticket does not need); any production import between core and the adapter layer; the\npriority map (`config.py` has NO priority copy — verified: no priority attribute exists on the module,\nso there is no third priority literal to pin).\n\n## Testing\n\nThe oracle is the parity test itself, and it must be shown to have teeth rather than asserted to:\nre-run the mutation above and confirm the new test goes RED, then revert and confirm GREEN. A parity\ntest that passes against a divergent map is worse than none.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] a test in `state/test_config.py` asserts `config.local_to_jira_status` equals\n      `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` loaded from `adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py` via the existing\n      `_load_attr` helper — full-dict equality, not a per-key spot check\n- [ ] MUTATION-CHECKED: with `config.local_to_jira_status[\"deleted\"]` changed to a non-workflow value\n      the new test FAILS, and with it reverted the test PASSES; both verdicts recorded on this ticket\n- [ ] `config.py` carries a lock-step comment naming the canonical map and the enforcing test, in the\n      same form as the existing `jira_to_local_status` comment\n- [ ] `config.py` still imports nothing outside `__future__` — asserted by reading the diff; no\n      production dependency from core onto `adapters/`\n- [ ] the empty-dict kill-switch and operator-override behaviour are unchanged — the existing\n      `test_config.py` suite passes with ZERO edits to its existing tests (`git diff` shows only an\n      ADDED test)\n- [ ] `state/test_config.py`, `test_acli_status_resolution_heldout.py`, `test_jira_family_seam.py`\n      and `test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py` all pass","title":"config.local_to_jira_status is an unpinned third copy of the canonical Jira-family status map"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785618408075922001,"uuid":"b957775b-f0d7-4224-89f2-a16f4668b8fc"}